    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# 🚀 Setup Guide  \n**Author:** [AI INSIGHT Hub](https://www.youtube.com/@ainsighthub)\n\n---\n\n## 🔥 Firecrawl Setup  \n- **[Get 10% Off Firecrawl](https://firecrawl.link/ainsighthub )**  \n- Set up your **Firecrawl API credential** in `n8n` under **Credentials > HTTP Request**  \n- In your workflow, configure the **URL** or a **List of URLs** you want to extract content from\n\n---\n\n## 🧑‍💻 Self-Hosting?\nIf you're self-hosting n8n, you can use the Firecrawl **Community Node**:  \n👉 [n8n Firecrawl Community Node](https://www.npmjs.com/package/n8n-nodes-firecrawl?activeTab=readme)\n\n---\n\n✅ Once set up, Firecrawl will intelligently extract relevant content from the provided pages based on your workflow logic.\n",
        "height": 860,
        "width": 340
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1800,
        -480
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "2c110180-bf20-4e47-8cd3-08786fdf8534",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1/extract",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"enableWebSearch\": false,\n  \"ignoreSitemap\": false,\n  \"includeSubdomains\": false,\n  \"showSources\": true,\n  \"scrapeOptions\": {\n    \"formats\": [\n      \"markdown\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"ignoreInvalidURLs\": false,\n  \"urls\":{{ '[' + $('Loop Over Items').item.json.urls.map(url => `\"${url}\"`).join(', ') + ']' }} ,\n  \"prompt\": \"You are an AI assistant that analyzes raw HTML content of websites.   Your task is to extract detailed company information from the content.\\\\n\\\\n:mag: Look for:\\\\n- Sections labeled **“About Us”**, **“Impressum”**, **“Kontakt”**, or **“Über Uns”**.\\\\n- If the page is in **German**, search for keywords like:\\\\n  - **\\\\\\\"Inhaber\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Geschäftsführer\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Vorstand\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Leiter\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Gründer\\\\\\\"**.\\\\n- If the page is in **English**, search for keywords like:\\\\n  - **\\\\\\\"Owner\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"CEO\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Founder\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Director\\\\\\\"**, **\\\\\\\"Manager\\\\\\\"**.\\\\n\\\\n:outbox_tray: For each person found, extract and return the following:\\\\n\\\\n- `owner_name`: Full name of the person (e.g. \\\\\\\"Max Mustermann\\\\\\\")\\\\n- `position`: Their role/title in the company (e.g. \\\\\\\"Geschäftsführer\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"CEO\\\\\\\")\\\\n- `company_name`: Full name of the company\\\\n- `email`: A contact email address associated with the company or person\\\\n- `url`: The page URL (e.g. Impressum or Kontakt page URL)\\\\n\\\\n:package: Output Format:\\\\nReturn a **JSON array of objects**, like this:\\\\n\\\\n[\\\\n  {\\\\n    \\\\\\\"owner_name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Full Name\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"position\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Position Title\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"company_name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Company Name\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"contact@example.com\\\\\\\",\\\\n    \\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://example.com/impressum\\\\\\\"\\\\n  }\\\\n]\\\\n\\\\n:pushpin: Notes:\\\\n- Return **all relevant individuals**, not just the most senior.\\\\n- If no valid information is found, return an **empty array**: `[]`\\\\n- **Do not** include any text or explanation outside of the JSON array.\",\n  \"schema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"owner_name\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"adress\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"position\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"email\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"url\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"owner_name\",\n      \"adress\",\n      \"email\",\n      \"url\"\n    ]\n  }\n}",
        "options": {
          "redirect": {
            "redirect": {}
          }
        }
      },
